<title>USA: IBM's Whiteside to head BBN venture - WSJ.</title>
<headline>IBM's Whiteside to head BBN venture - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp executive John Whiteside, considered a rising star at the company, resigned to head an electronic commerce venture owned by Andersen Consulting and BBN Corp, the Wall Street Journal said in Tuesday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>Whiteside had worked on building IBM's global communications network, the paper said.</p>
<p>Insiders believed he was on his way to becoming a top manager at the company, it said.</p>
<p>The venture, called ServiceNet, was set up last year.</p>
<p>--New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
